@* Explanation panel for the FLUX path. There is only ever ONE copy of the order, so there is
   no "typed vs stored" split to show — every edit reached the store the moment it was made. *@
@inherits FluxorComponent
@inject IState<OrderState> OrderState

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-header">Where the data actually is</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <h6>In the store — one copy, read by every page</h6>
        <p class="mb-1">Name: <code>@OrderState.Value.CustomerName</code></p>
        <p class="mb-1">City: <code>@OrderState.Value.City</code></p>
        <p class="mb-1">Quantity: <code>@OrderState.Value.Quantity</code></p>

        <div class="alert alert-light border mt-3">
            The URL carries nothing. Back and Forward move you between pages, but there is no
            older copy of the order for them to replay — every page reads this same state.
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0">
            <strong>One limit worth knowing.</strong> This store lives in server memory for your
            current connection. Back and Forward are safe, but pressing <strong>F5</strong> or
            reopening the app starts a new connection and the store resets to its initial values.
            Surviving a reload needs storage that outlives the connection — that is a later topic.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
